# a `.typedef` marker declares the type of a FIELD. Written as a unit-level
# definition it is the construction such a definition cannot hold -- which the
# bare form was already refused as, while parentheses hid it: the definition
# was accepted and every use of the name reached the emitter as an unhandled
# binding (E0500), including a union arm, which skipped the box rule as well.
Arr2: (array t: i64 to: 2).typedef
Bare: i64.typedef
main: function is {
    rs: Arr2
    x: Bare
    print "\{rs.length} \{x}"
}
